# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the context root's
# .dockerignore, so this trims the session-capture build context only and
# leaves the repository's other images (dockerfile, script/Dockerfile.release,
# script/Dockerfile.arm) building against the unfiltered context they expect.
#
# Nothing here is read by the build: cargo target directories are outputs, the
# node trees belong to the frontend/agentvis web builds this image skips, and
# the history is ~850 MB of context transfer for no layer.
**/target
**/node_modules
.git
